 for any integer $Q\le e^{N^{\rho}}$ such that
$(Q, q_{j, s})=1$, for all $j\in M^c$ and $s\in\mathbb{N}_{\beta_j}$. 

Recall that, according Remark \ref{rem:1}, in our case $\eta=\phi*\psi$ for some two smooth functions
$\phi, \psi$
supported in $(-1/(8d), 1/(8d))^d$.  Therefore, by the Cauchy--Schwarz inequality we only need to prove
